    "title": "Kendrick Lamar – i",
    "text": "What did Kendrick Lamar say about \"i\"?Lamar told Rolling Stone in June 2015 that he wrote the song to encourage positivity: I’ve woken up in the morning and felt like shit,” he says. “Feeling guilty. Feeling angry. Feeling regretful. As a kid from Compton, you can get all the success in the world and still question your worth. […] My partner Jason Estrada told me, ‘If you don’t attack it, it will attack you.’ If you sit around moping, feeling sad and stagnant, it’s gonna eat you alive. I had to make that record. It’s a reminder. It makes me feel good. According to Songfacts, Kendrick told 93.7 The Beat: The record feels great; it feels good, but it comes from a place of depression. It comes from a place of insecurity. Not only for [other people], but for myself. It’s a lot of things that I deal with personally. That you deal with, that everyone in this room deals with. So, it touches on so many different things, as far as equality within us as human beings, and accepting one another. People that wanna commit suicide; people that just don’t respect themselves or like the way they look, feel, talk, dress, and not accept who they are. We all put on this world to be kings, and walk in his image, and that’s how it starts – that song.",
